Step 1: Create the Project
1. Open Visual Studio 2019.
2. Click Create a new project.
3. Select ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework).
4. Click Next.
5. Project Name:SecureMVCApp
6. Click Create.
7. Select:
   - ASP.NET Core Web App (Model-View-Controller)
   - Change Authentication → Individual User Accounts
8. Click Create.
Visual Studio automatically creates the Identity database, Login, Registration, Logout and Identity models.     Practical 5
Step 2: Run the Application
Press:
Ctrl + F5

The home page should open.
At the top-right, you should see:
Register
Login

Step 3: Register a User
Click Register.
Enter:
Email: student@gmail.com
Password: Student@123
Confirm Password: Student@123

Click Register.
The user is saved in the AspNetUsers table.     Practical 5
Step 4: Verify the User
Go to:
View → Server Explorer
Open:
Data Connections
→ DefaultConnection
→ Tables
→ AspNetUsers

Right-click AspNetUsers → View Data.
You should see the registered user.
Step 5: Create Secure Controller
Right-click:
Controllers
→ Add
→ Controller

Create:
StudentController.cs

Use:
using System.Web.Mvc;

namespace SecureMVCApp1.Controllers
{
    public class StudentController : Controller
    {
        public ActionResult Index()
        {
            return View();
        }
    }
}
The important part is:
[Authorize]

It protects the controller so that only logged-in users can access it.     Practical 5
